    "body": "Before hinge fields can be compared, the source bundle and exported GLB must be shown to refer to the same declarations. C266 adds an isolated source/program/object provenance binding prerequisite using pinned C265, C261 and permitted C257 utilities.\n\nIt checks canonical source identity, complete object sets and both repeated mapping records against source-derived facts. It supports correctly rebound changed inputs and rejects stale, sparse or contradictory provenance. Hinge values, complete joint sets, ordered endpoints and historical admission remain unqualified.\n\nThis recovery publishes the preserved candidate results, all ten previously ignored logs, independent audits and bounded closure guidance. The published candidate passed ten groups, 222 methods, fourteen corpus bindings and 748 expected C266 outcomes. Independent review and exact-input audits approve reuse; fresh workflow/documentation checks pass. Product runtime, pinned predecessors, fixtures, adopted contracts, budgets and hosted workflows are unchanged.\n\nMerge must target exact head 665d344a118ac2f6689e13dbafdff99b480a02d3. Resulting-main checks, branch disposition and the required saved handoff/external receipt remain to be completed after integration. Scope: #258. Do not start another milestone.",
